╰┈➤ Soo ippudu veta aypoindi veta elaa chesamo let's Understand every column::
-- customer_id: customer_id BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT
Purpose: Gives every customer a stable identity
          Cannot be NULL
          Cannot be negative
          Is automatically generated
          Is the primary key
-- Ikkada do not use an email address as the primary key endukante Emails can change, are larger than numeric identifiersand expose business data throughout relationships

-- full_name: full_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
-> VARCHAR(100) stores variable-length text up to the declared limit
-> NOT NULL means the value must be present.

-- email: email VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
-> The unique constraint prevents two customer rows from using the same email: CONSTRAINT uq_customers_email UNIQUE (email)
-- Application validation may check this first, but the database remains the final authority

-- phone: phone VARCHAR(20) NULL
Telephone numbers are identifiers, not quantities. You do not add, subtract, or average telephone numbers. They may also contain country codes, leading zeros, spaces, or formatting characters

-- status: status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE'
When an insert omits status- MySQL supplies ACTIVE
-> Later we will improve how valid status values are controlled chupisthanu ok

-- Timestamps: created_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP -- Records creation time
updated_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
    DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP -- Automatically changes when the row is updated

